menu "Camera stream (components/camera)"

    config CAMERA_HTTP_PORT
        int "HTTP port of the camera server"
        range 1 65535
        default 80
        help
            The server answers on the Wi-Fi address: http://<address>/stream (MJPEG) and
            /snapshot.jpg. Only while the camera is switched on in Settings > Camera.

    config CAMERA_MAX_FPS
        int "Frames per second at most"
        range 1 30
        default 5
        help
            The sensor runs at 30 frames/s; only as many frames as this are compressed and sent.
            Every frame goes over Wi-Fi through the ESP32-C6, which also carries the rest of the
            network traffic, so keep it low (docs/CAMERA.md).

    config CAMERA_JPEG_QUALITY
        int "JPEG quality (10-95)"
        range 10 95
        default 50
        help
            Higher is sharper and larger. The frame size shows in Settings > Camera.

    config CAMERA_HMIRROR
        bool "Mirror the picture left to right"
        default n
        help
            The module's picture is mirrored: text reads backwards (board, 2026-10-13). The PPA
            mirrors it while scaling (not the sensor's mirror bit, which would shift the Bayer order
            the ISP expects). At 1920x1080 this adds a PPA pass over the full picture. Untested.

    config CAMERA_MAX_VIEWERS
        int "Stream connections at most"
        range 1 3
        default 2
        help
            go2rtc on the server takes one and serves every other viewer, so 2 leaves one for a
            browser. Each connection sends every frame again over Wi-Fi.

endmenu
